{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/46535-changeling-the-lost-vs-the-dreaming-compatibility-rules","id":46535,"title":"Changeling The Lost vs. The Dreaming compatibility rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T15:20:43-08:00","id":46535,"title":"Changeling The Lost vs. The Dreaming compatibility rules?","content":"Please let me know if this belongs in the OWoD/CWoD subforum. I knkw the rules are probably too different to mesh properly, but are there any rulesets (homebrew, probably, but, like, that anyone has put online, for example) to allow Changeling the Lost and Changeling the Dreaming characters to play within the same session? If the answer is anything remotely like a &quot;yes&quot;, my intent is to see if I can pit the Lost team against the Dreaming team, or at least reflavour the fey from C:tL to feel more like Dreaming changelings. I haven't much experience with the games, so if the premises are as difficult to intermesh with the rules (I know that Dreaming is about making the world wonderous enough to survive in and all that, but I'm a bit fuzzy on the point of Lost more specifically than &quot;get out of the hands of the Fair Folk, one way... [austere tone]or another[/tone]&quot;), this may be completely fruitless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","name":"JET73L","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:55:55-08:00","id":46899,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as I know there is no strictly crossover material, but...<br /> <br /> ...there's a nWoD conversion of Dreaming in MrGone collection:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_Conversion.doc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_Conversion.doc\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_Conversion.doc\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_Conversion.doc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_nWOD_sheet_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_nWOD_sheet_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_nWOD_sheet_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/fansheets/CtD_nWOD_sheet_2.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> and two nWoD card with no rules attached to them (no idea if they're compatibile with published conversion):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/WorldofDarknessSheet(Changeling).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/WorldofDarknessSheet(Changeling).pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/WorldofDarknessSheet(Changeling).pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/WorldofDarknessSheet(Changeling).pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/NWoD_Changeling.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/NWoD_Changeling.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/NWoD_Changeling.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/NWoD_Changeling.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then, there's a conversion made by zenten on google docs:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19v5ptN99MhNRnH8vX94soHH7vYFcWcxDzTE8rg-ljfE/pub\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19v5ptN99MhNRnH8vX94soHH7vYFcWcxDzTE8rg-ljfE/pub\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19v5ptN99MhNRnH8vX94soHH7vYFcWcxDzTE8rg-ljfE/pub\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/19v5ptN99MhNRnH8vX94soHH7vYFcWcxDzTE8rg-ljfE/pub </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All nWoD games are &quot;compatibile&quot; with each other so that should do what you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can also look trough Dreams of Delirum by Angelus Michaels:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/71845074/Dreams-of-Delirium\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/71845074/Dreams-of-Delirium\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/71845074/Dreams-of-Delirium\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scribd.com/doc/71845074/Dreams-of-Delirium </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> it started as nWoD darker reimagination of Dreaming/Dark Ages Fae and then converted to Lost supplement.<br /> <br /> And there's this thing from a week ago:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/196005781/Changeling-the-Lost-House-Rules\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/196005781/Changeling-the-Lost-House-Rules\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/196005781/Changeling-the-Lost-House-Rules\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scribd.com/doc/196005781/Changeling-the-Lost-House-Rules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no idea what exactly it is, it seems to be something new, at least for me - anyway, it does have a fluff and rules for &quot;Dreamers: The Exiled&quot;, so that also may be what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> I hope that at least some of this material may help you.<br /> <br /> Good luck and let us know how it turned out :]<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T09:53:05-08:00","id":46949,"title":"","content":"Where the fluff is concerned, there are some routes to adopt each game as (one of) the other's antagonist. the Lost, for example, have an antagonist group called 'the Banished' which are True Fey exiled from Arcadia, somehow able to survive in the material world - they function a lot like the changelings do, but with slightly off things about them like having unique kiths and different contract progression. Fae are typically banished by breaking a pledge which includes banishment, or they choose to leave when they have lost all of their titles and, rather than risk oblivion, hide in the mortal realm. They often wish to return and seek a way to, but are either unable or are too weak to survive. The ones who choose to leave may try to build themselves up as changelings do until they have the power to steal a title from another True Fae, and claim a realm again. This group seems like a ripe choice to replace with Changeling the Dreaming characters.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about CtD, but a friend much more familiar with it suggested to me that the Autumn People could be adapted into fetches. As she described them, when a person gets taken by the Dreaming and becomes a changeling, reality responds to the loss of that person by creating one with a huge amount of banality. If that were to be presented as &quot;when someone gets taken by the fae, a false person, heavily infused with reality, gets left behind with powers to counteract the fae&quot;, then it might work. It would make the already very personal conflict the fetch represents more potent and potentially unifying as an antagonist.<br /> <br /> Finally, from my trolling on the White-Wolf wiki, I found a CtD group called <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dauntain\" target=\"_blank\">Dauntain</a> which could maybe be adapted as the Lost themselves. From what I understand, they are changelings, most often victims of a Ravaging, who can't cope with the Fae or the Dreaming, and embrace reality, and who hunt down changelings after a Ravaging happens. That can be presented as, &quot;people who were unwilling made into fae by being taken to nightmarish realms wherein they endured torture, and, once escaped, tried to reclaim their humanity and protect others from that threat&quot; - which is clearly the Lost, and possibly close enough to apply to the Dauntain.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, to me at least, it looks like there are three conceptual places where the two games can be tinkered with to fit together. Here is a rundown of the CtL setting, which may present some issues to be resolved:<br /> - Arcadia still exists and is still accessible. People get taken there all the time, and the in-between realm of the Hedge is frequently used by all sides (except fetches I guess).<br /> - The True Fae of Arcadia are presented as &quot;living narratives&quot; to an extent; they collect Titles from the stories (and dreams) of mankind, and act out &quot;plays&quot; to suit those Titles and claim new ones. Often, they need actors and props for their plays; sometimes they just want to live like nobility, who need servants. Their primary antagonists are each other, and they battle through narratives to steal Titles. Confederacies do form, but usually its 'every fae for itself' - selfishness to the point of not accepting others as real is part of their psychology.<br /> - People don't just spontaneously... Dream? become changelings via a change in their soul, as I understand it working in CtD. They are dragged to another world, forcibly altered, and escape. Time gets funky there, but one could say that it is a physical process of being taken and integrated into a Dream. The seasonal courts they form are said to protect them from the True Fae, in having a society to watch for and war against them, and by the protection of parts of reality which willingly change (and therefore is totally foreign to the fae), and in distinct methods each season advocates (acting with revelry instead of being the broken toys They expect, fighting back, learning their powers to use against the, and hiding too well to be found again).<br /> <br /> Not only is this a change in process, but it presents some quandaries for CtD characters. If they are banished True Fae, they probably took part in kidnapping and ravaging mortals at some point - and they probably want to again. They might have some of the philosophical perspectives from the Dreaming to justify this, and its a fact that not all Fae are horrible torturers (some Dreams are nice, after all; but you don't hear about realms no one wants to leave); they're going to be difficult to sympathize with, however.<br /> <br /> How I might present the Banished/CtD in a game like this is by emphasizing the purpose of Stories: they are tales to teach morality, virtue, social norms; they're inspirations; they're ways of understanding the world around you; they reflect the archetypes valued (or feared) in society. Stories, art, metaphor are things that make us Human, and make life worth living. I recommend using <a href=\"http://lyrics.wikia.com/Heather_Alexander:Storyteller\" target=\"_blank\">these lyrics</a> as a foundation, personally. True Fae are not only the stories that are, but the ones that may be, and the potential to tell them at all - if they go away entirely, a crucial aspect of humanity goes with them. Now, this doesn't make them nice - stories have some very twisted bad guys - and the Wyrd (the Storyteller) would probably prefer they have no concept of right and wrong in order to act out the stories correctly.<br /> The central conflict behind the Banished/CtD could be that... they lost, and they're not allowed to be stories anymore. That changes things in the narrative consciousness of mankind (or maybe it doesn't, and their personal loss is motive enough). When Cinderella gets her happily ever after in Arcadia, she also takes the Title of her evil stepmother - and gets to be both from now on. That's not how the story is supposed to go. Knights become dragons. Hactivists become Big Brother. The Ring was about to take Frodo's title, but Gollum stole the Ring - and when Frodo killed them both, he got to keep them forever. And then the victors, with all these new roles to play, go into other stories, and see what they can win. An Arcadia going down this path can be bloody bizarre, and might have some strange impacts on human psyches. And the Banished, just want to go back to the stories that were supposed to be. As much as the Evil Stepmother is not nice, letting Queen Cinderella be her (in addition to herself) is worse. [and, hey, that could get into some Once Upon a Time stuff - Cinderella becomes Snow White's evil queen, or something. Or hell, just use Once as a starting concept and ignore the last two paragraphs - that could work just as well.]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, there are some of my musings on the subject. I hope some of that is useful to you; I think some of that can make an interesting premise, especially when you have players in both groups - might be a little too PvP for my typical taste, but if there is a way to rally them to the same side, it would involve some interesting conflict and tension and clashing philosophy.<br /> <br /> Good luck to you, and I'd love to hear the ideas you end up using!<br /> ~Seraph Kitty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-11-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T11:26:19-08:00","id":46988,"title":"","content":"You can also use the optional truth about True Fae - they are human dreams so strong that they finally gained a existence in an abstract world. It's suggested in Autumn Nightmares IIRC. Take a look at short version on the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/True_Fae_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">wiki</a>. And it goes just as it says - &quot;without dreamers, there are no dreams.&quot; People stopped to dream about them and they got banished from Arcadia. Now they try to fill the world around them with wonder in order to survive and make people to dream about them once more, so they will be able to return to Arcadia. That would be the simpliest &quot;reflavour&quot; option you asked for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:38:35-08:00","id":47148,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Many thanks to both of you! I'm not only checking out the links, I already bookmarked this thread for further reference! SeraphKitty: Yeah, I figured Arcadia would be the world behind the Hedge, and that it would be glossed over or as a sequel to the events of a theoretical Dreaming scenario where someone re-opened the Hedge entrance to Arcadia (so the Dreaming isn't just spilling through, but there are ways in and out). You've got some good story ideas that go above and beyond my intent; I just wanted to play the childish, whimsical fey (the innocently psychopathic Fair Folk) in place of the coldly cruel (or viciously malevolent, or just plain human-eating and evil) fey of C:tL. Alexander: I might be able to work with that Autumn Nightmares suggestion, depending on the details. It's one of the few non-Mage splatbooks my local game shop consistently has in stock, so it should be easy to acquire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1963-jet73l","name":"JET73L","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}